# =============================================================================
# GALLO BASE DIESEL — environment variables
# =============================================================================
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (or `.env.local` for local overrides) and adjust.
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with `VITE_` to the client bundle.
#

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data Provider (PRD-005)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Selects which provider implementation `getDataProviders()` returns.
#
#   mock      → delegates every call to `src/mocks/api/*` (Fase 1, default)
#   supabase  → delegates to Supabase (Fase 2, PRDs 100+). All 34 providers are
#               implemented; the migration is env-only (no NotImplementedError).
#
# Switch is read at build time. Invalid values fall back to `mock` with a
# console warning in dev mode.
VITE_DATA_SOURCE=mock

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Auth Provider (PRD-107)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Selects which authentication backend <AuthProvider> uses. Independent from
# VITE_DATA_SOURCE so you can run real auth against mock data, or vice-versa.
#
#   mock      → pick-a-profile login backed by src/features/auth/mock-users.ts
#               (Fase 1, default). Password is ignored.
#   supabase  → real Supabase Auth (email/password). Resolves the user profile
#               from the `profiles` table and mirrors it for the mock data
#               scoping. Requires VITE_SUPABASE_* below.
#
# Read at build time; invalid values fall back to `mock` with a dev warning.
VITE_AUTH_SOURCE=mock

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase (Fase 2, PRDs 100+)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Connection settings for the Supabase data provider. Only consumed when
# VITE_DATA_SOURCE=supabase; the mock provider ignores them entirely.
#
# Both values are SAFE to expose in the client bundle:
#   - the URL is public;
#   - the publishable key (format: sb_publishable_...) is designed for the
#     browser and is gated server-side by Row Level Security (RLS).
#
# NEVER put the service_role / secret key here — it bypasses RLS and must stay
# server-only. Copy the real values into `.env.local` (gitignored), not here.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Service role key — SERVER/SCRIPT ONLY, used by `scripts/seed-supabase.ts` to
# bulk-seed the database (bypasses RLS). NO `VITE_` prefix so it is never bundled
# into the browser. Put the real value ONLY in `.env.local` (gitignored), NEVER
# here and NEVER in client code. Leave unset unless you are seeding.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copiloto de Vendas — posicionamento da superfície (PRD-025)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Onde a superfície do Copiloto aparece na tela de atendimento:
#
#   strip → faixa sobre o campo de digitação (default)
#   tab   → aba dedicada na Ficha do cliente
#   card  → card colapsável no topo da conversa
#
# Este valor é apenas o DEFAULT DE FÁBRICA (lido em tempo de build). Cada usuário
# pode sobrescrever em tempo de execução em Configurações → Copiloto (a escolha
# fica salva no localStorage, por navegador). Valor inválido cai em `strip` com
# aviso no console (dev).
VITE_COPILOT_PLACEMENT=strip
